# What Docker may read when it builds the image (the "build context").
# Deny everything, then allow only what the Dockerfile copies. Secrets and personal files can't
# reach the build, even by accident: .env, CVs (samples/cvs/), your job ads (samples/*.txt),
# results/ (runs, the cloud spend file) and the private learning notes.
*
!requirements.txt
!agents/
!prompts/

# Never, even inside the allowed folders:
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.env
.env.*
samples/
results/
docs/learning-notes.md
.venv/
.git/
